    <summary>Local zip password recovery for zip archives you own: dictionary and mask search on your PC, GPU support for WinZip AES, and a saved copy that opens without a prompt.</summary>
    <description>ZIP Password Recovery Software is a commercial Windows utility for zip password recovery on archives you own. It identifies whether a password protected zip archive uses ZipCrypto or WinZip AES, runs the search on the local machine and writes a copy of the archive with the password removed. For a fleet of PCs this suits support teams whose users regularly lose the password to their own old archives, since the work needs no upload to a web service.

![ZIP Password Recovery screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/zpr/zpr-v4-found.png)

## Before you install

This package installs the free trial of a commercial program. Full use needs a paid license, which is described in the trial section below. The installer includes the search engine and a starter word list, so no extra download is needed for the first run.

## How to start and recover zip password

1. Open the program and add archives through Add Files, or point Add Folder at a directory.
2. Set the destination in the Save to field.
3. Press Start. The search tries a word list first, then masks, and you can watch the progress of each archive.
4. If you remember the shape of the password, describe it as a mask to cut the search short.
5. After the program confirms a password, save the unprotected copy.

Trial note: the free trial performs the whole search and reports whether the password was found, while saving the decrypted archive is blocked in the unregistered version. A license removes that block.

![ZIP Password Recovery screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/zpr/zpr-v4-main.png)

## Who needs a zip password unlocker

- Help desk teams asked by staff to recover zip password access to a personal backup.
- Admins who meet a user who says they forgot zip password details for an archive made years ago.
- Offices that want a zip password unlocker which keeps every file inside the company network.

## Zip password recovery: hardware and time

ZipCrypto archives are quick on a processor. WinZip AES archives use a key derivation that a graphics card handles far better, so a workstation with a GPU finishes much sooner. Without one, the program still runs on the CPU and states in advance that the search may be long. Dictionary words and short masks are realistic. A long random password with AES-256 may never turn up. The program reads .zip files only, so a RAR or 7z archive needs another tool.

![ZIP Password Recovery screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/zpr/zpr-v4-searching.png)

## Trial and license

Full use of the program, including saving the recovered archive, requires a paid license from SoftOrbits. Plans on the site include a lifetime license, a one-year license and a business license for several machines. See [ZIP Password Recovery](https://www.softorbits.net/zip-password-recovery/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) for details.

[ZIP Password Recovery Software on Windows Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9PG498VDXQGK)

## FAQ: if you forgot zip password

### Is zip password recovery online safe for private files?

An online service means sending the whole file to a stranger's server, and an archive often holds tax papers or family scans. A local program keeps the file on your own disk, and there is no size limit set by an upload form.

### Is the ZIP password recovery download free?

The trial is free and runs the complete search, but saving the unprotected copy needs a paid license from SoftOrbits.

### How long does zip password recovery software take?

A ZipCrypto archive or a common word takes minutes. A long random AES password can run for days or end without a result, and the program shows an estimate before it begins.
